g these are  successes from the policy  the policies that were put in place  problems that we might well have had and  don't have because of the policies that  were undertaken  but  it is important to get inflation down um  to low and stable levels and that's the  fed's job mainly to accomplish although  uh for its part the white house the  biden administration is doing what it  can to also address for example high  energy prices by  releases from the strategic petroleum  reserve  doing what we can to make sure that we  relieve congestion at the ports but look  you know now you're seeing covered  lockdowns in china and um you know these  are factors really outside our control  that unfortunately threaten  to prolong supply chain disruptions that  um will affect our economy with  spillovers too  we've mentioned energy a couple times  and let's just talk there um uh  energy was already uh challenging and as  you noted since the war in uh between  russia and ukraine  uh the energy shock has only grown so  it takes a long time normally to to to  work through  supply issues when it comes to energy so  as you look out in the forecast how long  are we facing do you think roughly uh a  certain kind of energy crunch supply  crunch here it seems like that's  something liable to be with us here for  a while  well  i i agree  i mean  a reason why the president committed to  release a million barrels a day  from the strategic petroleum reserve was  to give american producers  time to ramp up production  but you know unfortunately i think most  producers of oil from shale  they experienced during the pandemic  very low prices and expected the  recovery to take a long time  and they actually cut production rather  than  ramping it up and so um it really is  necessary to see supplies increase um in  the meantime we we have um the releases  from the strategic petroleum reserve  that have helped um you know there's  also a very strong desire around the  world  to  make sure that um r